{'post_id': 682, 'day': 252, 'content': 'unpopular opinion: AI tools are only as good as their support 🚨\n\njust got passed between 3 different support teams on the same ticket. THREE. used to work with tools where one person actually owned your issue start to finish. now it\'s like playing hot potato with my problem\n\nNovaMind\'s assistant is solid for ideation work but if something breaks? good luck. the product does what it says but the support experience is giving "we scaled too fast" energy\n\nmight go back to my old workflow tbh. cheaper peace of mind > fancier features that come with support roulette 💀\n\n#AITools #FreelancerLife #SupportMatters'}
{'post_id': 681, 'day': 252, 'content': "tried getting into NovaMind last week and... yeah the onboarding is rough 😅 docs are scattered, tutorials assume you already know what you're doing, and the UI has like 47 different menus. spent more time clicking around than actually creating. \n\nfor early-career folks like me trying to learn this thing, it's frustrating. there's potential here but the learning curve is steep af. wish they had a guided setup or at least a coherent getting-started path instead of throwing everything at you at once.\n\nmight come back to it when i've got more bandwidth, but rn it feels like too much friction for what should be intuitive. #SaaS #ProductFeedback"}
